{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41699606",
      "title": "Managing Multi-Component State with the Context API",
      "sourceHash": "c9218ea8f71dcef6e21bf4bb712e1ab20d730a83c8f139adb2f5064af6af6be3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "So let's make sure that, by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 7.2,
          "en": "those items here are not open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.2,
          "end": 9.45,
          "en": "And instead we can open them by clicking on them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.45,
          "end": 12.993,
          "en": "making sure though that only one item is open at most.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 17.13,
          "en": "Now since we're working with multiple components here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "to make sure that every component on its own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 23.31,
          "en": "is highly configurable in a very easy way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.31,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "Since we're doing that, we can't add the logic directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "inside the Accordion component, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 34.56,
          "en": "because there we can't easily interact with the children",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.56,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "because the children can be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "We're not rendering them inside of this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 41.4,
          "en": "we're just forwarding them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.4,
          "end": 44.01,
          "en": "We're forwarding the content that's passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.01,
          "end": 45.63,
          "en": "between the Accordion tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.63,
          "end": 48.363,
          "en": "between those </ul> tags in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 52.71,
          "en": "nonetheless, we can add the core logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.71,
          "end": 56.88,
          "en": "for controlling which item is open to that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.88,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "We can do that with help of React's context feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 63.96,
          "en": "with its context API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.96,
          "end": 68.96000000000001,
          "en": "So we can import { createContext } from 'react';",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.24,
          "end": 71.46000000000001,
          "en": "and call createContext here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 74.91,
          "en": "and then create an AccordionContext.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.91,
          "end": 79.02,
          "en": "And I'm deliberately doing that here in that same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.02,
          "end": 82.35,
          "en": "where I created the Accordion component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 85.203,
          "en": "because now I'm not trying to build some context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.203,
          "end": 88.47,
          "en": "that should be usable in all kinds of places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.47,
          "end": 91.77,
          "en": "of the entire app, but instead I'm building a context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.77,
          "end": 95.25,
          "en": "that's directly tied to this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.25,
          "end": 99.96000000000001,
          "en": "and all other related Accordion components as you'll see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.96000000000001,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "because now here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 104.34,
          "en": "instead of directly returning the on unordered list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.34,
          "end": 108.13,
          "en": "we can return the AccordionContext.Provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 112.953,
          "en": "wrapped around the unordered list like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 115.35,
          "en": "and set the value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.35,
          "end": 117.963,
          "en": "just as you learned it earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.28,
          "end": 122.28,
          "en": "Now the value that should be set will be managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.28,
          "end": 124.08,
          "en": "by this Accordion component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.08,
          "end": 126.81,
          "en": "So this component now basically also acts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.81,
          "end": 129.153,
          "en": "as the provider for this context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 132.48,
          "en": "Now, the value I wanna set here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.48,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "for my context should be an object, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 139.56,
          "en": "which in the end contains the id of the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 141.24,
          "en": "that should currently be open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.24,
          "end": 142.67000000000002,
          "en": "So the openItemId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.85,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "because again, it should only be one item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 147.96,
          "en": "that's open at the same time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.96,
          "end": 150.15,
          "en": "so we can manage it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.15,
          "end": 152.19,
          "en": "We wanna store the id of the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 153.78300000000002,
          "en": "that should currently be open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 156.66,
          "en": "Now, initially this can be null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.66,
          "end": 159.72,
          "en": "because initially no item should be open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.72,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "And then I also want to add two functions here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 165.06,
          "en": "inside of that Accordion component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 167.49,
          "en": "One function that could be called openItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 171.513,
          "en": "for, well, setting a new openItemId in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.53,
          "end": 175.92000000000002,
          "en": "and one function that can be called closeItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.92000000000002,
          "end": 179.013,
          "en": "which will set the openItemId back to null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.343,
          "end": 184.05,
          "en": "Therefore, the openItemId should be dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.05,
          "end": 188.34,
          "en": "and hence we can use the useState hook from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.34,
          "end": 193.34,
          "en": "and import that to manage the openItemId here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.98,
          "end": 195.39,
          "en": "with that state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.39,
          "end": 197.16,
          "en": "So the openItemId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.16,
          "end": 201.093,
          "en": "and a set openItemId state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.8,
          "end": 205.82999999999998,
          "en": "Now, initially we have no open id here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.82999999999998,
          "end": 207.51,
          "en": "but the openItem function here should receive the id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.845,
          "end": 213.81,
          "en": "of the item, which should now be opened as a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.81,
          "end": 216.01,
          "en": "and therefore here we can call setOpenItemId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.05,
          "end": 220.743,
          "en": "and pass that id to that state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.73,
          "end": 224.48,
          "en": "And here in closeItem, we can call setOpenItemId(null).",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227.97,
          "end": 230.79,
          "en": "Now down here for the context value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.79,
          "end": 235.79,
          "en": "we can store the openItemId state here as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 241.533,
          "en": "for that openItemId key in the context value object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.64,
          "end": 244.59,
          "en": "And in addition, we can,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.59,
          "end": 247.713,
          "en": "and should add a pointer to the openItem function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.78,
          "end": 251.46,
          "en": "We could do it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.46,
          "end": 253.65,
          "en": "or since we have the same name on both sides,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.65,
          "end": 255.48,
          "en": "use that shortcut.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.48,
          "end": 258.43,
          "en": "We can also do that for the openItemId by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.86,
          "end": 262.323,
          "en": "and also add the closeItem function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.16,
          "end": 266.61,
          "en": "And that's now the context value that should be distributed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.61,
          "end": 268.953,
          "en": "to all interested components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.06,
          "end": 274.14300000000003,
          "en": "but which components are interested here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.01,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "Now the components interested in that context value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 282.75,
          "en": "of course, are the other Accordion components that are meant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 282.75,
          "end": 286.74,
          "en": "to work together with that wrapping Accordion component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.74,
          "end": 290.01,
          "en": "so in this case the AccordionItem component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.01,
          "end": 293.613,
          "en": "since that is the only other Accordion component we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.57,
          "end": 299.57,
          "en": "In here, we now wanna rate that Accordion context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 301.26,
          "end": 304.14,
          "en": "and to simplify this process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 304.14,
          "end": 307.02,
          "en": "and also make it a bit more secure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 307.02,
          "end": 309.84,
          "en": "I'll actually start by adding a custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 309.84,
          "end": 312.06,
          "en": "to the Accordion component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 312.06,
          "end": 314.01,
          "en": "I'll export another function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 314.01,
          "end": 315.81,
          "en": "which is called useAccordionContext.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 317.58,
          "end": 319.653,
          "en": "So that will be a custom hook here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.73,
          "end": 323.52,
          "en": "And the idea behind that custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 323.52,
          "end": 327.94,
          "en": "is to use the built-in useContext hook in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 328.86,
          "end": 331.05,
          "en": "and read that AccordionContext",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 331.05,
          "end": 333.48,
          "en": "and get hold of that context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 333.48,
          "end": 337.95,
          "en": "But of course here, since I'm exporting it, it is possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 337.95,
          "end": 341.13,
          "en": "that in theory, this hook here could be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 341.13,
          "end": 342.54,
          "en": "in some other component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 342.54,
          "end": 345.003,
          "en": "that's not wrapped by the Accordion component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 346.02,
          "end": 348.12,
          "en": "and that therefore doesn't have access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 348.12,
          "end": 349.68,
          "en": "to the AccordionContext",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 349.68,
          "end": 351.63,
          "en": "because it therefore wouldn't be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 351.63,
          "end": 353.973,
          "en": "by the provider of that context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 355.47,
          "end": 357.87,
          "en": "That's why inside this custom hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 357.87,
          "end": 360.33,
          "en": "I'm checking if not context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 360.33,
          "end": 363.57,
          "en": "So if this is undefined, if we weren't able to connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 363.57,
          "end": 367.98,
          "en": "to that context because the wrapping provider is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.98,
          "end": 370.03,
          "en": "and in that case we could throw an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 371.37,
          "end": 373.89,
          "en": "so that if we or some other developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 373.89,
          "end": 376.14,
          "en": "who might also be working on that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 376.14,
          "end": 378.3,
          "en": "uses this hook in the wrong place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 378.3,
          "end": 380.88,
          "en": "we throw an error telling the developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 380.88,
          "end": 383.61,
          "en": "that this Accordion component must be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 383.61,
          "end": 386.94,
          "en": "as an extra wrapper around whichever component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 386.94,
          "end": 388.89,
          "en": "wants to use this hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 388.89,
          "end": 390.633,
          "en": "That's an extra safety measure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 392.13,
          "end": 394.89,
          "en": "So here we could then output an error message of,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 394.89,
          "end": 397.59000000000003,
          "en": "'Accordion-related components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 397.59000000000003,
          "end": 402.59000000000003,
          "en": "must be wrapped by <Accordion>', something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 403.62,
          "end": 405.33,
          "en": "Now, after this check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 405.33,
          "end": 407.1,
          "en": "and this error being thrown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 407.1,
          "end": 409.26,
          "en": "we can then return that context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 409.26,
          "end": 411.603,
          "en": "And here we know that it will exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 412.59000000000003,
          "end": 414.84000000000003,
          "en": "Therefore, now in AccordionItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 414.84000000000003,
          "end": 417.9,
          "en": "we can now use this useAccordionContext hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 417.9,
          "end": 422.9,
          "en": "we just added, importing it from the Accordion.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 423.63,
          "end": 426.39,
          "en": "And then here we can use the structuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 426.39,
          "end": 430.2,
          "en": "to pull out the parts that are interesting to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 430.2,
          "end": 433.053,
          "en": "And in that case, that is the openItemId,",
